// BT-4515 (ADR 0145 § 2): a class that defines its own `then:`, as a promise
// type would. `Object >> then:` is not sealed, so this one wins: its block
// gets the resolved value, not the receiver. See then_test.bt.

Value subclass: ThenPromise
  field: resolved :: Integer = 0

  then: aBlock :: Block(Integer, Object) -> ThenPromise =>
    ThenPromise resolved: (aBlock value: self resolved)
